---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="About | Victor Pass"
    description="I'm Stephen Smithwick. Victor Pass is my company: one engineer, in Colorado Springs."
>
    <section class="banner">
        <img
            src="/images/cheyenne-mountain.webp"
            srcset="/images/cheyenne-mountain-1000.webp 1000w, /images/cheyenne-mountain.webp 2000w"
            sizes="100vw"
            alt="Cheyenne Mountain rising above a quiet road in Colorado Springs"
            fetchpriority="high"
        />
    </section>

    <article class="container page">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>

        <h1 class="display">Victor Pass</h1>

        <p class="lede">
            I'm Stephen Smithwick. Victor Pass is my company — one engineer, in
            Colorado Springs.
        </p>

        <h2>Background</h2>

        <p>
            Twenty years of building backends: distributed systems and
            infrastructure at Amazon and Snowflake, platform and principal
            engineering before that in Sydney. Kinesis, SageMaker, DynamoDB, and
            a long tail of things that had to stay up.
        </p>

        <p>
            These days most of my attention is on local LLMs, agent tooling, and
            the unglamorous problem of getting the right context in front of a
            model.
        </p>

        <p>
            Victor Pass is small on purpose. I'd rather take on focused jobs and
            do each one properly than build you something overly-complicated.
        </p>

        <h2>How I work</h2>

        <p>
            In the open, further upstream than is comfortable. Ideas get a page
            while they're still speculative, and when I abandon something I say
            so and leave the page up, because "I tried this and it didn't work"
            is more useful to the next person than silence.
        </p>

        <p>
            My blog,{" "}
            <a href="https://stephensmithwick.github.io/">CodeVantage</a>, has
            nine years of this: forty-odd posts, most of them thinking out loud.
        </p>

        <h2 id="work">Working with me</h2>

        <p>I'm interested in problems, not leads.</p>

        <p>
            If some part of your work is slow, manual, or held together by a
            spreadsheet nobody else wants to touch, I'd like to hear about it.
            No pitch attached, and I'm not going to try to sell you software on
            a first conversation. I'm local and happy to come to you.
        </p>

        <h3>How it usually starts</h3>

        <ol>
            <li>Email me about the problem. A few sentences is enough.</li>
            <li>
                We talk, in person if you're local. No charge, and no pitch.
            </li>
            <li>
                If there's something worth building, I'll suggest a small first
                step before anything bigger.
            </li>
        </ol>

        <p>
            <a class="button primary" href="mailto:work@victorpass.dev">
                work@victorpass.dev
            </a>
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>

        <p>
            New work:
            <a href="mailto:work@victorpass.dev">work@victorpass.dev</a>
            <br />
            Everything else:
            <a href="mailto:hello@victorpass.dev">hello@victorpass.dev</a>
        </p>
    </article>
</Layout>

<style>
    .banner {
        position: relative;
        height: clamp(240px, 42vh, 460px);
        overflow: hidden;
        background: var(--ink);
    }

    .banner img {
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        object-fit: cover;
        object-position: 50% 42%;
    }

    .banner::after {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
        background: linear-gradient(
            to top,
            rgb(10 20 18 / 45%),
            transparent 45%
        );
    }

    .caption {
        position: absolute;
        inset: auto 0 1rem;
        z-index: 1;
        margin: 0 auto;
        color: rgb(255 255 255 / 75%);
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        text-align: right;
        text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .page {
        max-width: calc(46rem + 2 * var(--gutter));
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding-top: 4.5rem;
        font-size: 1.075rem;
    }

    .lede {
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
    }

    h2 {
        margin: 3.5rem 0 0.75rem;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    #work {
        scroll-margin-top: 6rem; /* clear the sticky header */
    }

    p,
    li {
        line-height: 1.75;
    }

    a:not(.button) {
        color: var(--accent);
        font-weight: 600;
        text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    }
</style>
